1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,893
Categories color-code your events so you can read a week at a glance,

2
00:00:04,893 --> 00:00:07,903
and filter them so you can hide what you don't need.

3
00:00:07,903 --> 00:00:11,744
This video shows how an event gets its color, how to make categories

4
00:00:11,744 --> 00:00:15,533
and put events in them, how to filter the calendar by category, and

5
00:00:15,533 --> 00:00:17,920
what happens when a category is deleted.

6
00:00:22,520 --> 00:00:26,324
Every event is drawn in one color, chosen in this order.

7
00:00:26,324 --> 00:00:30,802
The event's own color comes first, when you tick Use its own color.

8
00:00:30,802 --> 00:00:33,440
Next comes the color of its category.

9
00:00:34,190 --> 00:00:38,337
An event with neither takes the color of its kind of event, such

10
00:00:38,337 --> 00:00:40,233
as a meeting or a holiday.

11
00:00:40,233 --> 00:00:42,780
Last comes the color of its calendar.

12
00:00:46,980 --> 00:00:49,406
Open Calendars, then Categories.

13
00:00:49,406 --> 00:00:54,575
The list shows your categories, and the shared ones with an Everyone badge.

14
00:00:54,575 --> 00:00:59,171
Company holiday and Training are shared, so everyone can use them.

15
00:00:59,171 --> 00:01:00,830
Choose Add category.

16
00:01:01,282 --> 00:01:05,120
Give the category a Name and a Color, and choose Save.

17
00:01:05,120 --> 00:01:09,341
Maria makes Sales calls, in orange, and Admin work, in gray.

18
00:01:09,341 --> 00:01:12,667
These two are hers, and nobody else sees them.

19
00:01:12,667 --> 00:01:15,802
Both then appear in the list, ready to use.

20
00:01:17,409 --> 00:01:21,718
People who can manage all calendars also see Everyone can use it.

21
00:01:21,718 --> 00:01:24,266
Tick it, and the category is shared:

22
00:01:24,266 --> 00:01:28,210
everyone sees it and can use it, such as a company holiday.

23
00:01:28,210 --> 00:01:32,579
Only people who manage all calendars can change a shared category.

24
00:01:36,776 --> 00:01:41,667
In the event editor, Category lists your categories and the shared ones.

25
00:01:41,667 --> 00:01:45,618
Maria picks Sales calls for her customer lunch and saves.

26
00:01:45,618 --> 00:01:49,256
The event is now drawn in the color of its category.

27
00:01:49,707 --> 00:01:52,282
Another event can keep its own color.

28
00:01:52,282 --> 00:01:56,595
The pricing workshop is also in Sales calls, but Use its own color

29
00:01:56,595 --> 00:01:58,392
is ticked, with a green.

30
00:01:58,392 --> 00:02:01,567
The event's own color wins over its category's.

31
00:02:02,309 --> 00:02:06,260
Events with no category and no color of their own, like the pipeline

32
00:02:06,260 --> 00:02:10,159
review, keep the color of their kind of event or of their calendar.

33
00:02:14,355 --> 00:02:20,137
The calendar lists your categories under Categories, with No category at the end.

34
00:02:20,137 --> 00:02:22,995
Untick a category to hide its events.

35
00:02:22,995 --> 00:02:27,315
Here Sales calls disappears, and ticking it brings it back.

36
00:02:27,765 --> 00:02:32,043
Untick No category to hide every event that has no category.

37
00:02:32,043 --> 00:02:38,135
Your choice is remembered in this browser, so the calendar opens the same way next time.

38
00:02:42,326 --> 00:02:46,943
To delete a category, open its Actions menu and choose Delete, then confirm.

39
00:02:46,943 --> 00:02:50,659
The events that used it are kept, and they show again in the

40
00:02:50,659 --> 00:02:54,826
color of their kind of event, unless they have a color of their own.

41
00:02:56,826 --> 00:03:00,456
Make a category for each kind of work, put events in it, and

42
00:03:00,456 --> 00:03:02,216
filter the calendar by it.

43
00:03:02,216 --> 00:03:03,646
Thanks for watching.

